==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|undoutedly}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|undoubted|ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʌnˈdaʊtɪdli/}}
* {{hyph|en|un|doubt|ed|ly}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-undoubtedly.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# Without doubt; [[definitely]].
#* {{RQ:Orczy Miss Elliott|chapter=The Ayrsham Mystery|passage=The cane was '''undoubtedly''' of foreign make, for it had a solid silver ferrule at one end, which was not English hall–marked.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|indubitably}}
* {{l|en|unquestionably}}
* {{l|en|doubtlessly}}
* {{l|en|undoubtably}}
* {{l|en|without a doubt}}

